Both deliverables are in place, the tool fix is confined to the one proven defect, and the whole suite is green. Summary of what I did:

**Changed files (all inside the allowed write set)**
- `packaging/public-plugin/plugin.schema.json` (new) — draft 2020-12 **locally authored subset** mirroring exactly the builder's manifest constraints: the ten top-level keys, `additionalProperties: false` at every level, `schema` const, `skills` pinned to the eight exact names (8 items, unique, enum), publisher/icon objects with required fields, `release` shape. Its `description` states it is a LOCALLY AUTHORED SUBSET, that it is NOT the official vendor schema, and that the vendor schema/validator remain `NOT_EXECUTED`. Its bytes are digest-pinnable via `official_schema_sha256`.
- `tests/test_public_plugin_packaging.py` (new) — 19 stdlib `unittest` cases, temp-dir fixtures, no network, never touching the real tree, all driving the real `build_plugin(...)`/`freeze(...)` (and `main()` for the exit-code case). Symlink cases use the documented `_path_is_symlink` seam only when the host refuses real symlinks, so the real gate code always runs.
- `tools/build_public_plugin.py` — one proven defect fixed: `project_skill_md` never checked that the frontmatter `name` matches the skill directory, so case 3 ("wrong `name`") was not refused. It now raises `SKILL_FRONTMATTER_INVALID`. No other behavior changed.

